// floats) into shared memory ONCE per CTA, instead of reloading a fresh
// 81-float weight tile (with an associated bar.sync barrier) once per
// output channel inside the OC loop. Because the whole weight cache and
// the input tile are now fully resident in shared memory for the entire
// lifetime of the CTA and are never overwritten mid-loop, all 64
// iterations of the OC loop can run completely barrier-free, removing
// 63 redundant global-memory weight reload rounds and 127 bar.sync
// barriers per CTA compared to the previous version.
